Hatate (hatate-rs): a Rust rewrite of Hatate.

The application's own code is MIT licensed (LICENSE).

The Hatate AppImage bundles other software. Each component keeps its own licence; the texts are
in the image under usr/share/licenses/, and usr/share/licenses/INDEX.txt lists every component
with its version, licence and files:

  - Chromium (Chrome for Testing build, pinned in packaging/appimage/pins.toml): BSD-3-Clause for
    the Chromium project; the third-party components inside it are listed in the browser's own
    chrome://credits page. The proprietary Widevine CDM that ships in the archive is removed from
    the image.
  - GTK 4, libadwaita, GLib, Pango, Cairo, HarfBuzz and the other shared libraries the window
    links (mostly LGPL-2.1-or-later): the distribution packages' copyright files, under
    usr/share/licenses/lib/. LGPL libraries are shipped as separate shared objects in usr/lib/,
    so they can be replaced.
  - The Adwaita icon theme (LGPL-3.0 / CC-BY-SA-3.0).
  - The app's fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, texts under usr/share/licenses/fonts/) and DejaVu.
  - The Rust crates linked into the binaries: each crate's licence files under
    usr/share/licenses/crates/.
